id: rust.tokio-mpsc
kind: rust
title: tokio::sync::mpsc
aliases: mpsc, channel, queue, producer consumer
tags: async, channels, concurrency
questions:
  - how do tasks talk to each other in Tokio?
invariant: A bounded mpsc channel moves owned messages from many senders to one receiver, and a full channel makes send().await wait.
answer_30s: mpsc is the work-queue shape: many producers transfer ownership of each message to one consumer, and a bounded capacity turns a slow consumer into backpressure instead of growth.
answer_2m: |
  Boundedness is the design decision, not a detail: with capacity, send().await
  parks the producer when the consumer falls behind, so the pressure reaches the
  source; with an unbounded channel the failure is a memory graph that grows
  until the OOM killer resolves it. mpsc is also the ownership-transfer idiom:
  the message moves, so producer and consumer never share mutable state and no
  lock is needed. Closing is part of the protocol: when every sender drops, the
  receiver sees None -- the standard drain-and-exit signal for a worker.
when_to_use:
  - job queues, fan-in to a single owner, decoupling producers from consumers
avoid_when:
  - many consumers of the same message (broadcast) or only the latest value matters (watch)
minimal_example: |
  use tokio::sync::mpsc;

  let (tx, mut rx) = mpsc::channel::<Job>(256); // capacity = backpressure

  tokio::spawn(async move {
      while let Some(job) = rx.recv().await { // None when all senders drop
          if let Err(e) = handle(job).await { tracing::error!(%e, "job failed"); }
      }
      tracing::info!("queue drained, exiting");
  });

  tx.send(Job::new(payload)).await?; // waits when the queue is full
failure_modes:
  - an unbounded channel, so a slow consumer becomes an OOM
  - a sender cloned into a task that never drops, so shutdown is never observed
  - ignoring a send error after the receiver exited, losing the message
follow_ups:
  - how do you fan out one message to many consumers?
related:
  - rust.tokio-broadcast
  - rust.tokio-oneshot
  - design.bounded-queue
  - design.backpressure
  - design.producer-consumer
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/sync/mpsc/index.html
